[47;3H[?25h[m[?2026h[?2026l[?25l[38;2;153;153;153m[43;1H※ [1mrecap: [22m[3mI looked into why the bus list changes between runs: the list only shows buses that have left their first stop, so earlier-arriving buses pop in later. Next, you decide [m  [38;2;153;153;153m[3m[44;3Hhow not-yet-departed buses should appear, and I'll implement the fix. (disable recaps in /config)[47;3H[?25h[m[?2026h[?2026l[?25l[H                                                                                                                                                                                    [47;3H[?25h[?2004h[?1000h[?1002h[?1003h[?1006h[?2004h[?1000h[?1002h[?1003h[?1006h[?2004h[?1000h[?1002h[?1003h[?1006h[?2004h[?1000h[?1002h[?1003h[?1006h[?25l[H                                                                                                                                                                                      [38;2;177;185;249msrc/domain/buses.ts:91[m:                                                                                                                                                             [34mif [m(!first || !last || first.seconds > offset || offset > last.seconds) [34mcontinue[m;                                                                                                   [38;2;177;185;249mbusesInService [mskips any trip that hasn't reached its first departure time yet, and the sheet's list is built from its output. That was meant for placing buses on the map, since   a trip that hasn't started has no position to show. But it also means the list never shows a bus that's still waiting at its terminus.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                  I replayed the real weekday timetable through the same rule. "App" is the current list; "timetable" is what the next 4 arrivals really are:                                                                                                                                                                                                                             ┌─────────────────────┬──────────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐[K
  │     Stop @ time     │          App shows           │                                            Missing                                            │                              ├─────────────────────┼──────────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤[K
  │ Casa do Sal @ 08:00 │ S1 1m, U3 6m, S1 16m, [1mS1 36m[22m │ U3 → República in [1m6m[22m (leaves Coimbra B 08:05), U3 → Coimbra B in [1m10m[22m (leaves República 08:02) │                              ├─────────────────────┼──────────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤                              │ Casa do Sal @ 08:10 │ S1 6m, S1 26m, S1 47m        │ U1 in [1m6m[22m, S1 → Serpins in [1m11m[22m, U3 in [1m12m[22m                                                      │[K
  ├─────────────────────┼──────────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤                              │ Serpins @ 08:00     │ 2 buses                      │ the 08:20 S1 and the 08:50 S2 departures                                                      │[K
  └─────────────────────┴──────────────────────────────┴───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘                            
[K
  This matches what you saw: open the app at 08:00, then again at 08:03 after the U3 has left Coimbra B, and a bus arriving sooner than ones already listed "appears". It also        happens while the app stays open, since the list recalculates every second. Over every stop in 5-minute steps from 06:00 to 22:00 on a weekday, the list's first bus was missing    or wrong in [1m12.1%[22m of cases (882 of 7,296).[K
                                                                                                                                                                                      [1mTwo related side effects[22m[K
[K
  1. [1mEnd-of-line stops only list buses arriving to finish there.[22m At Coimbra B at 08:00, the app shows 4 buses, all ending at Coimbra B. The departures you could actually board (U1 
     → Vale das Flores 08:15, S1 → Serpins 08:20) never appear, because a trip is never "heading to" its own first stop. [38;2;177;185;249mdirectionsAtStop [m([38;2;177;185;249msrc/domain/directions.ts:22[m) also ignores     first-stop calls, so the direction filter at these stops is affected in the same way.[K
  2. The list is cut to 4 rows ([38;2;177;185;249msrc/ui/sheet/ApproachingBuses.tsx:8[m), so a bus 36 minutes away can fill a row that belongs to one 6 minutes away.                                                                                                                                                                                                                         [1mHow to fix it[22m                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                           Build the list from the timetable, separately from which buses are on the map:[K
  - The sheet lists the next scheduled calls at the stop, including trips that haven't started (optionally within a time limit). At an end-of-line stop, that includes buses leaving    from there, and buses that finish there are probably left out.[K
  - The map keeps showing only buses in service, or shows a not-yet-started bus at its first stop marked "departs 08:15".                                                             - A new test covers a stop where the soonest bus hasn't left its first stop yet.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                        This fits the empty [38;2;177;185;249mplays/010-data-validation [mplay, if that's where you want it. How to show a bus that hasn't left yet ("in 6 min" or "departs 08:15") and whether buses that      finish at the stop stay in its list are your calls. Tell me and I'll write the intent and implement it.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                               [38;2;153;153;153m✻ Baked for 2m 44s · done 10:45                                                                                                                                                     [m
